{"id":"rondonia","name":"Rondônia deforestation arc","country":"Brazil","story":"Dry-season (Jul–Oct) clearing fires along the Amazon arc of deforestation.","places":["Rondônia","Porto Velho","Ariquemes"],"lang":["pt"],"bbox":[-64.5,-11.8,-61.0,-8.5],"grid_deg":0.1,"data_through":"2026-11-13","built_at":"2026-11-14T05:08:34+00:00","estimand":{"primary":"Calibrated vegetation-hotspot estimate on the Aqua MODIS scale per period: the Aqua-scale equivalent expected from the observed MODIS and VIIRS sensors. Day and night are calibrated separately and added. This is a model-based estimate, not a direct MODIS measurement after 2002.","why_aqua":"The early-afternoon orbit is the only one observed continuously from 2002 (Aqua) through Suomi-NPP, NOAA-20 and NOAA-21. A common Aqua scale makes the long record comparable, but discards VIIRS-only detail; the native VIIRS and raw series are therefore published beside it.","model_scope":"The 2000-11…2002-06 segment is a Terra-only extrapolation fitted to Aqua and inherits that link's measured hold-out bias. After the measured MODIS acquisition-time/archive change, the published estimate uses the VIIRS chain only, still on the 2002–2020 Aqua scale.","secondary":["Fire cell-days (0.1° cell × UTC day with ≥1 detection), Aqua scale","Hotspots on the Suomi-NPP VIIRS scale (modelled before 2012)","Persistent heat sources (kilns, flares, industry, volcanoes) harmonized separately","Raw detections — not comparable across satellite eras"],"not":"Not burned area and not a count of fires: a detection is one hot pixel in one overpass."},"method":{"acquisition_time_shift":"The MODIS archive's reported daytime acquisition time shifts by more than 15 minutes after the measured onset while Terra shifts the other way and VIIRS stays fixed. This is an archive/reporting-time change, not a physical sun-synchronous orbit shift; from the onset MODIS is omitted when VIIRS observes and the change is published as its own step/placebo test.","drift":"Yearly satellite-to-satellite ratios use the same calendar months in every year, so a changing month mix cannot look like drift.","confidence_filter":"Drop VIIRS 'l' and MODIS confidence <30. This is a class-level crosswalk, not a numeric one; the two filters remove different shares and the sensitivity is reported.","static_mask":"0.01° cells where science-quality FIRMS `type` is 1–3 for ≥50% of ≥3 detections. The mask is computed over the full archive and applied to every period. NRT rows have no `type`, so outside this mask they are assigned to vegetation by construction; their share is published.","coverage":"share of days each satellite delivered data anywhere on Earth in each period (measured, so launches, gaps and the Suomi-NPP end come from the data); below 25% a satellite is left out, otherwise counts are divided by coverage","calibration":"ratio of totals per calendar month, day and night separately, shrunk toward the pooled ratio by empirical Bayes (shrinkage strength estimated from the data). Chain: Terra→Aqua (2002–2020, bridges 2000–2002 only), Suomi-NPP→Aqua (2012–2020, pre-drift), NOAA-20→Suomi-NPP, NOAA-21→NOAA-20; chain-closure mismatch is added to the error. The validation table shows when a seasonal factor does not beat a single ratio or the identity estimator; estimator choice is not selected on the outer hold-out.","combination":"inverse-variance mean of the satellites observing each period (calibration error + counting noise, evaluated at the pooled mean). The conformal widening factor is fitted on a VIIRS-only MODIS-denial reconstruction; out-of-sample coverage is reported rather than assumed to be exactly 95%.","comparison":"each period vs the same month/week in other complete years: median, ratio, percentile, rank — no sigma thresholds (fire counts are skewed)","weekly":"ISO-8601 weeks; weeks use their Thursday's month calibration; a leading partial ISO week is never used as a complete baseline","provisional":"periods containing near-real-time rows are provisional: FIRMS replaces NRT with standard processing after ~3 months, and the mirror keeps only one of the two, so the NRT-to-standard difference cannot be measured from it. NRT rows also lack FIRMS `type`; untyped heat anomalies outside the static mask remain in the vegetation series and their share is published.","witnesses":"Each fire case is heard by independent witnesses: the harmonized satellite record, a MODIS-against-VIIRS cross-check, NASA EONET, GDACS and the press. A witness that could not see says so, so a missing report is never read as 'no fire'.","exposure":"Population (WorldPop 2020, 1 km) and infrastructure (OpenStreetMap) inside the 0.1 degree cells where the record shows fire. A context layer, not an impact estimate: there is no fire perimeter, no smoke and no fire spread here."},"calibration":{"veg_det_D":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[5.2013,3.9352,4.6761,2.7718,3.5936,3.0739,2.8649,2.6117,3.4184,4.5387,4.8051,6.5847],"pooled":3.2442,"sigma2":0.4012,"tau2":0.1244,"n_periods":218,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_SNPP","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2012-02","2020-12"],"beta":[0.1816,0.2193,0.3209,0.2104,0.1826,0.2331,0.27,0.2462,0.2454,0.1979,0.1918,0.2646],"pooled":0.2371,"sigma2":0.066,"tau2":0.0408,"n_periods":107,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA20","reference":"VIIRS_SNPP","window":["2018-05","2026-10"],"beta":[1.0215,1.0232,1.0227,1.0226,1.0119,1.0325,1.0268,1.0276,1.0139,1.0086,1.0536,1.0139],"pooled":1.0218,"sigma2":0.0378,"tau2":0.0002,"n_periods":97,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA21","reference":"VIIRS_NOAA20","window":["2024-02","2026-10"],"beta":[0.7537,0.7718,1.3198,0.9512,1.1708,0.9499,1.1021,1.0922,0.9907,1.2295,1.3211,0.6731],"pooled":1.0801,"sigma2":0.0025,"tau2":0.0916,"n_periods":31,"calibrated":true}],"veg_det_N":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[0.3841,0.441,0.5378,0.5213,0.4853,0.4105,0.4177,0.4